  "result": "`formatDuration(ms)` is now in `src/cli/duration.ts` and committed as `b1e68b2`. `npm run fast` passes (biome, boundaries, tsc and the related tests).\n\n- **Output:** `3_723_000` gives `1h 2m 3s`, `125_000` gives `2m 5s`, and `0` gives `0s`.\n- **Interior zeros:** these are kept (`1h 0m 5s`), since only leading zero units are dropped.\n- **Rounding and bad input:** sub-second values are floored. Negative or non-finite input returns `0s`.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/duration.test.ts` uses `node:test` and covers each of those cases.\n- **Shard weight:** the repo's shard-weight coverage test requires every test file to have an entry, so I added one to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Plan file:** I wrote the plan before coding at `.krn/duration-notes.md` and kept it updated. `.krn/` is gitignored, since the repo rules keep agent state there, so the notes are on disk but not in the commit.",
